// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`Cycle worlds in prompts > matches its snapshots > cycle-detailed 1`] = `
"# Build: Ripple background

## What I want
A calm, full-screen grid of small dots. When I click, a ring ripples out from that spot, pushing the dots outward and lighting them up in color as it passes. My cursor pushes nearby dots away. When nobody is interacting, ripples start by themselves every few seconds.

## Look
- Colors ("Spice Dunes" palette): background #E8C9A0, text #2A1405, secondary text #5E3517, accents #D9561A, #8C2F14, #2F6FA3.
- Where accent colors overlap, multiply them like ink on paper (canvas globalCompositeOperation "multiply").
- Slowly crossfade the whole page between these palettes, holding each for 8 seconds and blending in OKLab over about 1.5 seconds: "Spice Dunes": background #E8C9A0, text #2A1405, secondary text #5E3517, accents #D9561A, #8C2F14, #2F6FA3; "Abyss": background #021B2E, text #DDF7FF, secondary text #93BFD3, accents #00E6D2, #8B7DFF, #FF5FC8; "Toxic": background #10140A, text #F1FFD9, secondary text #B5C99A, accents #B6FF1A, #FF6A00, #9B5CFF; "Vapor Mall": background #F6E8FF, text #2B1240, secondary text #6A4C86, accents #FF71CE, #01CDFE, #B967FF.
- Keep all text readable at every moment of the crossfade (contrast at least 4.5:1).
- Font: "Anybody" from Google Fonts (variable width 50–150, weight 100–900), loaded with https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anybody:ital,wdth,wght@0,50..150,100..900;1,50..150,100..900&display=swap, with a system sans-serif fallback.
- The canvas is transparent over the background and cleared every frame. Size it for devicePixelRatio (capped at 2) and draw in CSS pixels.

## How it moves
- A full-screen canvas (100svh, at least 540px) holds a square grid of dots 26px apart (20px on screens under 700px wide): floor(width / spacing) + 1 columns and floor(height / spacing) + 1 rows, centered on the screen. Each dot remembers its rest position.
- Draw resting dots (glow under 0.08, or never touched by a ring) as circles of radius 1.3px in the secondary text color at 38% opacity, all in one path. Glowing dots get radius 1.3 + glow × 3.6px in their ring's color, one path per accent color, using the blend mode above.
- For each ring and each dot: k = (distance from the ring's center − age × ring speed) ÷ 60. If |k| < 2.5: g = e^(−k²) × e^(−age × fade), the dot is displaced outward from the ring's center by sin(k × 2) × g × push, and its glow target grows by g. The ring with the largest g colors the dot.
- A ring has a center, a start time and a color (the three accents in turn). It grows at 480px per second. Keep at most 8 rings (drop the oldest) and remove rings older than 5 seconds.
- Ring push is 20px.
- Ring fade is 0.55 per second (in e^(−age × fade)).
- When nobody has clicked for 3.5 seconds, start a ripple every 2.6 seconds (the first one right away) at a random spot: x = width × (0.2 + random × 0.6), y = height × (0.2 + random × 0.5).
- While the pointer is over the canvas, a dot whose rest position is within 120px of it is pushed away by s² × 22px (s = 1 − distance / 120), its glow target grows by s × 0.6, and if that is its strongest effect it takes the second accent color.
- Each frame, every dot eases 25% of the way to its rest position plus its displacement, and its glow eases 25% of the way to min(glow target, 1.4). Its color index updates whenever something colors it, and stays otherwise.
- Run one requestAnimationFrame loop. dt = seconds since the last frame, clamped to 0.05; t = seconds the loop has run (the sum of dt). Ring start times and ages use t.
- A click lands between frames: its ring starts at the previous frame's t.
- Rebuild the grid on every resize (all dots back to rest).
- Automatic ring positions call Math.random() for x, then y.
- Reduced-motion still frame: two rings from (width / 2, 45% of the height), 0.9s and 0.35s old, in the first and second accent, with no easing (dots jump straight to their displaced position and glow).

## How people interact
- Click or tap (on release): a ring at that point, which also counts as the latest click for the automatic ripples.
- pointermove and pointerdown on the canvas make the pointer active (a finger only while it is down); pointerleave and pointercancel make it inactive.

## Where this goes
Create a single index.html file with all CSS and JavaScript inline, ready to open by double-clicking it. Don't use any libraries or build tools.

## Rules
- Smooth on a mid-range laptop and a phone: one requestAnimationFrame loop, batched canvas drawing, devicePixelRatio capped at 2, pause when off-screen.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion: start paused and show a meaningful still frame, with a visible Play/Pause button.
- Accessible: real buttons, visible keyboard focus, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, decorative canvases hidden from screen readers.
- Works on touch screens without blocking vertical scrolling.

## When you're done
I'm new to coding. When you're done: 1) tell me in simple steps how to open the page in my browser, 2) explain in two or three sentences how it works, 3) suggest three small changes I could ask you for next."
`;

exports[`Cycle worlds in prompts > matches its snapshots > cycle-quick 1`] = `
"# Build: Ripple background

A calm, full-screen grid of small dots. When I click, a ring ripples out from that spot, pushing the dots outward and lighting them up in color as it passes. My cursor pushes nearby dots away. When nobody is interacting, ripples start by themselves every few seconds.

Colors: background #E8C9A0, text #2A1405, secondary text #5E3517, accents #D9561A, #8C2F14, #2F6FA3. Font: "Anybody" from Google Fonts.
Crossfade every 8 seconds between backgrounds #E8C9A0, #021B2E, #10140A, #F6E8FF.
- Ring speed: 480px/s
- Ring push: 20px
- Auto ripple every: 2.6s

One index.html file, CSS and JS inline, no libraries.
Keep it smooth, accessible, and respectful of reduced motion."
`;

exports[`blackhole prompt > is deterministic and matches its snapshots > detailed-existing-experienced 1`] = `
"# Build: Black hole

## What I want
A black hole in the middle of the screen. A faint grid around it bends into a funnel, and glowing particles drift in, orbit faster as they get close, stretch into streaks and vanish at its edge. I can press and hold to drag the hole around, and clicking releases a burst of new particles.

## Look
- Colors ("Doomsday" palette): background #1E1412, text #F1E6DC, secondary text #BFAEA1, accents #FF3B1F, #FF9F1C, #B5E61D.
- Where accent colors overlap, add them so they glow (canvas globalCompositeOperation "lighter").
- Font: "Anybody" from Google Fonts (variable width 50–150, weight 100–900), loaded with https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anybody:ital,wdth,wght@0,50..150,100..900;1,50..150,100..900&display=swap, with a system sans-serif fallback.
- A full-screen canvas (100svh, at least 540px), transparent over the background and cleared every frame. Size it for devicePixelRatio (capped at 2) and do all math in CSS pixels.

## How it moves
- Keep 1200 particles (500 on screens under 700px wide). Start each at a random spot on the canvas (Math.random() for x, then y). A particle that crosses the event horizon, or gets farther from the hole than the screen's diagonal, starts again off-screen: angle = random × 2π, then distance = half the screen's diagonal × (1 + random × 0.3) from the hole.
- Behind everything, a grid of lines 40px apart: vertical lines at x = width ÷ 2 + k × 40 for every whole k with −40 ≤ x ≤ width + 40, running from y = −40 to height + 40, and horizontal lines the same way. Draw each as a polyline with a point every 40 ÷ 3 px. Pull each point toward the hole: with d = its distance from the hole and R = the horizon radius, move it toward the hole by 3 × mass × R² ÷ (d + R), but never past the hole's center. Stroke all lines as one path, 1px wide, in the soft text color at opacity 0.3.
- The event horizon is a circle of radius 40px around the hole; a particle that gets closer than that is swallowed. Draw it last: filled with the background color, then its edge as a 2px line in the first accent color. When the blend mode above is lighter, give the edge a soft glow first: stroke it 4 times with lighter blending, 2 + 12, + 9, + 6 and + 3 px wide, at opacity 0.0375, 0.075, 0.1125 and 0.15.
- Draw each particle as a line from position − velocity × 3 to position, 1.5px wide with round caps, batched into one path per color: the first accent within 2.5 × R of the hole, the second within 6 × R, the third farther out, using the blend mode above.
- The hole's mass is 1. Each frame, for each particle, with (dx, dy) = hole − particle and r = its length: velocity += (dx, dy) ÷ r × 2000 × 1 ÷ r² × f; then velocity ×= 0.998^f; then position += velocity × f.
- Whenever a particle starts (or starts again) with (dx, dy) = particle − hole and r = its length, its velocity is 1 × √(2000 × mass ÷ r) × (−dy, dx) ÷ r px per frame, sideways to the hole, so it orbits; drag makes the orbits shrink until it falls in.
- Pressing and holding drags the hole: a press counts once it has lasted 0.2s (a finger must also hold still for 0.25s, so swipes still scroll); each frame hole += (pointer − hole) × (1 − (1 − 0.12)^f).
- A click or tap (on release, from a press shorter than 0.2s) releases 80 particles there: take the next 80 particles in turn (cycling through the list) and restart each at that point, moving in a random direction (angle = random × 2π) at random × 4 px per frame.
- Run one requestAnimationFrame loop. dt = seconds since the last frame, clamped to 0.05; f = min(dt × 60, 2.5).
- The hole starts in the middle. Each frame, in this order: handle clicks, move the hole, move the particles, draw (grid, particles, hole).
- Place the particles again on every resize.
- Reduced-motion still frame: the scene after 180 frames of the physics with f = 1 and no pointer.

## How people interact
- The canvas has touch-action: pan-y, so swipes still scroll.

## Where this goes
First, look at my project's files and figure out what framework and styling it uses. Add this as a component that fits how the project is already built. Don't change unrelated files. When you finish, tell me which files you added or changed and how to put the component on a page.

## Rules
- Smooth on a mid-range laptop and a phone: one requestAnimationFrame loop, batched canvas drawing, devicePixelRatio capped at 2, pause when off-screen.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion: start paused and show a meaningful still frame, with a visible Play/Pause button.
- Accessible: real buttons, visible keyboard focus, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, decorative canvases hidden from screen readers.
- Works on touch screens without blocking vertical scrolling.

## When you're done
Keep the explanation short: list the files and the key parameters I can tweak."
`;

