exports[`halftone prompt > is deterministic and matches its snapshots > detailed-existing-experienced 1`] = `
"# Build: Halftone paper

## What I want
A sheet of small gray halftone dots. Around my cursor the dots swell, push outward and split into three inks, slightly out of register like a riso print; moving fast exaggerates the misprint. Clicks send rings rolling through the dots, and when I leave it alone the swell wanders by itself.

## Look
- Colors ("Riso" palette): background #F4F2FF, text #1A1240, secondary text #4E4777, accents #EC1C7F, #2A47EA, #FF7A00.
- Where accent colors overlap, multiply them like ink on paper (canvas globalCompositeOperation "multiply").
- Font: "Anybody" from Google Fonts (variable width 50–150, weight 100–900), loaded with https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anybody:ital,wdth,wght@0,50..150,100..900;1,50..150,100..900&display=swap, with a system sans-serif fallback.
- Size the canvas for devicePixelRatio (capped at 2) and do all math in CSS pixels.

## How it moves
- A full-screen canvas (100svh, at least 540px), transparent, cleared every frame, covered in a honeycomb grid of dots with spacing g = clamp(short side ÷ 30, 18, 30) px: rows 0.866 × g apart, ceil(width ÷ g) + 2 columns and ceil(height ÷ (0.866 × g)) + 2 rows, dot (i, j) at ((i − 0.5) × g + (j odd ? g ÷ 2 : 0), (j − 0.5) × 0.866 × g). A plain dot has radius base = 1.1 + g × 0.035; draw all plain dots as one path in the soft text color at opacity 0.5.
- The swell has radius R = short side × 34%. For each dot at distance d from the swell's center: e = q × q × (3 − 2q) with q = 1 − d ÷ R when d < R, else 0.
- Dots with e below 0.04 stay plain. The rest (e capped at 1.25) are hot: pushed away from the swell's center by e × g × 0.55 and with radius base + e × g × 0.4.
- Hot dots are printed three times, once per accent, with the blend mode above, after the gray dots. Ink L (0, 1, 2) is moved by (fixed + slip × (L − 1)) × e and drawn 0.08 × L smaller (radius × (1 − L × 0.08)), where fixed = (−1, −0.6), (1, −0.2) and (0, 0.95) × g × 0.1 for L = 0, 1, 2, and slip = the swell's velocity × 1.1, each axis clamped to ±g × 0.6.
- The swell's center follows a target each frame: new = lerp(center, target, 1 − (1 − 0.13)^f); its velocity = lerp(velocity, (new − center) ÷ f, 1 − (1 − 0.2)^f); then center = new. The target is the pointer while it is over the canvas (a finger while it touches); otherwise it wanders: (width × (0.55 + 0.3 × sin(t × 0.27)), height × (0.42 + 0.2 × sin(t × 0.41 + 1))).
- A click or tap (on release) starts a ring there with radius 0 and strength 1; each frame radius += 11 × f and strength ×= 0.968^f, and it is removed below 0.03. A ring adds strength × exp(−u²) × 0.9 to every dot's e, with u = (the dot's distance from the ring's center − radius) ÷ (g × 1.7), for |u| < 3.
- Run one requestAnimationFrame loop. dt = seconds since the last frame, clamped to 0.05; f = min(dt × 60, 2.5); t = seconds the loop has run (the sum of dt).
- Rebuild the dot grid on every resize; the swell starts (once) at 64% of the width and 40% of the height, at rest.
- Reduced-motion still frame: the swell resting where it starts, toward the upper right.

## How people interact
- The canvas has touch-action: pan-y, so vertical swipes still scroll.

## Where this goes
First, look at my project's files and figure out what framework and styling it uses. Add this as a component that fits how the project is already built. Don't change unrelated files. When you finish, tell me which files you added or changed and how to put the component on a page.

## Rules
- Smooth on a mid-range laptop and a phone: one requestAnimationFrame loop, batched canvas drawing, devicePixelRatio capped at 2, pause when off-screen.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion: start paused and show a meaningful still frame, with a visible Play/Pause button.
- Accessible: real buttons, visible keyboard focus, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, decorative canvases hidden from screen readers.
- Works on touch screens without blocking vertical scrolling.

## When you're done
Keep the explanation short: list the files and the key parameters I can tweak."
`;

