- Each letter has a stretch vector V (in px, starting at 0). Draw it as: translate(center + V / 2), rotate(θ), scale(1 + |V| ÷ font size, (1 + |V| ÷ font size)^−0.5), rotate(−θ), where θ is V's angle; so it lengthens toward the pull, one end staying put, and thins out sideways. While a letter is held, V eases toward (pointer − where it was grabbed) × 1, by 0.35 × f of the way each frame, never longer than 2.5 × the font size.
- Released letters spring back: velocity = (velocity − V × 0.2 × f) × 0.9^f; V += velocity × f, so they overshoot and wobble until they settle.
- Run one requestAnimationFrame loop. dt = seconds since the last frame, clamped to 0.05; f = min(dt × 60, 2.5).
- Lay the word out again on every resize and once the Anybody font has finished loading.
- Reduced-motion still frame: every letter at rest except the middle one (index floor(count ÷ 2)), caught mid-wobble with V pointing straight up at 0.35 × max stretch × font size.

## How people interact
- Press on a letter (inside its box) to grab it: a mouse at once, a finger after holding still for 0.25s, so swipes still scroll (touch-action: pan-y). Release lets go. Draw the held letter last.

## Where this goes
Write this as a single React component file (.jsx, or .tsx if my project uses TypeScript) with no extra libraries. Include a short usage example.

## Rules
- Smooth on a mid-range laptop and a phone: one requestAnimationFrame loop, batched canvas drawing, devicePixelRatio capped at 2, pause when off-screen.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion: start paused and show a meaningful still frame, with a visible Play/Pause button.
- Accessible: real buttons, visible keyboard focus, text contrast of at least 4.5:1, decorative canvases hidden from screen readers.
- Works on touch screens without blocking vertical scrolling.

## When you're done
I'm new to coding. When you're done: 1) tell me in simple steps how to open the page in my browser, 2) explain in two or three sentences how it works, 3) suggest three small changes I could ask you for next."
`;

